(FIL-53: Read line includes the trailing newline when one is present.
 Also covers: FIL-46 (Read line REPLACES the buffer, not appends) - the
 two claims are asserted by the SAME number: a fixed-length seed is
 appended to the sink buffer first, then Read line's result is checked
 to be EXACTLY the written line's length plus one (the newline). If
 Read line appended instead of replacing, the size would be seed length
 + line length + 1, not line length + 1 - so this one assertion puts
 both claims on trial at once, the same reasoning D2's own probe used
 for the plain `Read` claim.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-53.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   10
   11
 Then with the post-read check changed to `is not 21` (seed length +
 line length, the WRONG "append" answer), to prove a failing assertion
 is classified correctly:
   ASSERT FIL-46: expected 21 got 11
 exit code 95.
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called 'the postbag' at "vf_scratch/files/fil53.txt".
Write "helloworld\n" to 'the postbag'.
Close 'the postbag'.
open a file for reading called 'the postbag' at "vf_scratch/files/fil53.txt".
a buffer called 'the pallet' is 64 bytes in size.
append "PRESEED123" to 'the pallet'.
If 'the pallet's size is not 10 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-46: expected 10 got {'the pallet's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the pallet's size.
Read line from 'the postbag' into 'the pallet'.
If 'the pallet's size is not 11 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-46: expected 11 got {'the pallet's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the pallet's size.
Close 'the postbag'.
